4.1 FlatBuffers (or Protobuf) schemas (packages/schemas)

Tick (top-of-book + micro-depth):

message TopOfBook {
  string market = 1;           // e.g., "BTCUSDT", "BTCINR", "USDTINR"
  double bestBid = 2;
  double bestBidQty = 3;
  double bestAsk = 4;
  double bestAskQty = 5;
  DepthLevel depthBid[5];      // optional, K<=5
  DepthLevel depthAsk[5];      // optional
  int64  ts_exchange_ns = 6;   // if available
  int64  ts_gateway_ns = 7;    // gateway arrival
}
message DepthLevel { double px = 1; double qty = 2; }


MarketMeta:

message MarketMeta {
  string market = 1;                // "BTCUSDT" etc.
  string base = 2;                  // "BTC"
  string quote = 3;                 // "USDT"/"INR"
  uint32 pricePrecision = 4;
  uint32 quantityPrecision = 5;
  double minQty = 6;
  double minNotional = 7;
  double maxQty = 8;
}


Decision / OrderBundle:

message OrderBundle {
  string triangleId = 1;      // e.g., "BTC:STRAIGHT"
  string route = 2;           // "STRAIGHT" | "REVERSE"
  Leg legs[3] = 3;            // sequential
  double expectedEdge = 4;    // after fees
  double capitalINR = 5;      // starting INR for the route
  string riskToken = 6;       // per-bundle id for hedges/cancels
  int64  ts_engine_ns = 7;
}
message Leg {
  string market = 1;
  string side = 2;            // "BUY" | "SELL"
  double price = 3;           // market/IOC -> price=best±ε
  double qty = 4;             // after rounding & minQty check
  string timeInForce = 5;     // "IOC" | "FOK" | "GTC"
  string intent = 6;          // "TAKER"
}


Execution reports:

message Execution {
  string clientOrderId = 1;
  string market = 2;
  string side = 3;
  double price = 4;
  double qty = 5;
  double fee = 6;
  string feeAsset = 7;
  string status = 8;          // NEW|PARTIAL|FILLED|CANCELED|REJECTED
  string riskToken = 9;
  int64  ts_ack_ns = 10;
}

4.2 Gateway (Node) public API (internal)

POST /orders → place single order

POST /bundles → place 3-leg bundle (sequential)
Body: OrderBundle
Behavior: submits leg-1, waits for ack/fill ≥ threshold, then leg-2, then leg-3; if any leg fails or slips, hedge → close exposure using opposite side on same market.

GET /balances

GET /markets → list meta

WebSocket private: receive Execution + balance updates.

For Cursor: generate gateway-node/src/server.ts with these routes and a Broker class that translates OrderBundle → REST calls + private socket listeners.

4.3 Engine (Rust) IPC

UDS path: /tmp/arb_engine.sock

Frames: FlatBuffers messages TopOfBook (gateway→engine) and OrderBundle (engine→gateway)

Backpressure: bounded MPSC channels (size 4096). Drop stale ticks by market (keep latest only).